Give base's ETW redirectors names of their own, so they stop colliding with
winwrap at link time.

base/trace_event/trace_event_etw_export_win.cc defines functions called
EventRegister, EventWrite and EventUnregister -- and, since patch 05,
EventWriteTransfer -- which forward to advapi32 through GetProcAddress. They
are ordinary external symbols under the system's own names:
_EventRegister@16 and so on.

winwrap 0.4.9 began defining every function it redirects under its plain name
as well as its __imp_ slot, for callers that reference a function by name. All
of those names live in one object, plain_names_<arch>.obj, which is an
ordinary archive member: nothing is extracted until something references one
of them. Something does. base calls SHGetKnownFolderPath (base_paths_win.cc,
win_util.cc), which the SDK declares without dllimport, so the reference is to
the plain name and that object is what answers it. With it come winwrap's
EventRegister, EventUnregister and EventWriteTransfer, and the link fails:

  winwrap.lib(plain_names_x86.obj) : error LNK2005: _EventRegister@16 already
  defined in base.lib(trace_event_etw_export_win.obj)

Up to winwrap 0.4.8 this did not happen, because the plain SHGetKnownFolderPath
was defined on its own in shell32.cc and brought nothing else along. Patch
05's note that the two "do not conflict" was true of that version.

The fix is four #defines ahead of the include of chrome_events_win.h, renaming
the functions to base_EventRegister and so on. The declarations in evntprov.h,
the calls the mc-generated header makes, and the definitions in this file are
all renamed together, so nothing else changes: base still resolves the real
functions with GetProcAddress, still returns 0 where they are absent, and its
call sites still bind to its own definitions. It just no longer claims the
system's names for them. This holds with or without winwrap in the link.

--- a/base/trace_event/trace_event_etw_export_win.cc
+++ b/base/trace_event/trace_event_etw_export_win.cc
@@ -23,6 +23,18 @@
 // implement these functions locally instead of using the import library, and
 // can therefore still run on Windows XP.
 #define EVNTAPI __stdcall
+// Not in the original. The four redirectors below are given names of their
+// own, so that they are this file's and nobody else's. Under the system's
+// names they are external symbols called EventRegister and so on, and a
+// library that also defines those -- winwrap does, for callers that reference
+// the functions by name -- then collides with them at link time. Defined
+// ahead of the include so that evntprov.h's declarations, the calls
+// chrome_events_win.h generates, and the definitions below all take the new
+// names together. The GetProcAddress strings are untouched, being strings.
+#define EventRegister base_EventRegister
+#define EventWrite base_EventWrite
+#define EventUnregister base_EventUnregister
+#define EventWriteTransfer base_EventWriteTransfer
 // Include the event register/write/unregister macros compiled from the manifest
 // file. Note that this includes evntprov.h which requires a Vista+ Windows SDK.
 //
